Falsifies `system_tests::user::confinement_attack_tests::a_read_only_holder_cannot_send_and_an_ungranted_slot_names_nothing`.

Architecture: aarch64

The patch deletes the `WRITE` check on `Rendezvous::SEND` in `syscall::rendezvous::rendezvous_send`,
so a holder of `READ` alone sends: the right the capability lacks is taken from the method number
instead, which is claim 2's "userspace cannot forge a right" at the dispatcher, on the IPC fastpath
of §10 (the capability-based microkernel process model). A receiver is already parked, so the broken
gate delivers rather than blocking.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!` "a READ-only holder SENT: WRITE was forged from the method or an
argument register". Replayed on 2026-10-06 (UTC) by the milestone 633 (an outside agent attacks the
confinement claim) lane: red at exactly that assertion on aarch64.

Re-cut on 2026-10-12 (UTC) by lane maintainer/long-function-paydown-invoke, when the rendezvous
arms of `syscall::invoke` moved to `kernel/src/syscall/rendezvous.rs` for milestone 888 (a ratchet
on function length); the defect is unchanged. Replayed red at the same assertion on aarch64 that
day.

